# Project Rules

- Keep the core Python-first.
- Do not add Java as a core runtime.
- Add Rust/C++ only after profiling identifies a bottleneck.
- Keep modules behind the existing pipeline boundaries.
- Do not add hosted APIs or graph databases to the core path without an explicit task.
- Read `AGENTS.md` first.
- Use technical memory selectively: default to `docs/invariants.md`, `docs/schema.md`, the relevant module, and nearby tests.
- Read `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/evaluation.md`, `docs/design.md`, or `docs/decisions/*` only when the task needs that context.
- Use `rg` to locate symbols and call sites before opening long files.
